{"tag":"1UE0","kind":"statement","subkind":"theorem","paper":"2604.07243","version":"3","local":"thm-1","file":"","label":"thm:main","number":"1.1","section":"sec-1","order":1,"title":"Theorem","body_md":"\\label{thm:main}\nLet $R$ be a commutative ring.\n\n\\smallskip\n\\noindent\\textup{(1)}\nAssume that $2\\in R^\\times$ and let $\\Phi\\in\\{\\mathbf A_1,\\mathbf A_2,\\mathbf B_2\\}$.\nThen every locally inner endomorphism of $E_{\\mathrm{ad}}(\\Phi,R)$ is inner.\nMoreover, any locally inner endomorphism of $G_{\\mathrm{ad}}(\\Phi,R)$ is inner for\n$\\Phi\\in\\{\\mathbf A_2,\\mathbf B_2\\}$, and for $\\Phi=\\mathbf A_1$ under the additional assumption\nthat $E_{\\mathrm{ad}}(\\mathbf A_1,R)$ is normal in $G_{\\mathrm{ad}}(\\mathbf A_1,R)$.\n\n\\smallskip\n\\noindent\\textup{(2)}\nAssume that $2,3\\in R^\\times$.\nThen every locally inner endomorphism of $E_{\\mathrm{ad}}(\\mathbf G_2,R)$ is inner, and every locally inner\nendomorphism of $G_{\\mathrm{ad}}(\\mathbf G_2,R)$ is inner.\n\n\\smallskip\nIn particular, all groups listed above are $\\operatorname{Sha}$-rigid.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"thm","item":"statement/theorem","head":"environment","counter":"thm","number_from":"counter","labels":["thm:main"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"sha_rigidity_jgcc.tex","from":93,"to":112},"hash":"sha256:4692201967dbf03556c230f2ae1e2d092547dd51368f22f631917d39349e3cc4","minhash":"","census":"2604.07243v3#env-1","extractor":"ax/v0.5.19"}
{"tag":"IHHG","kind":"statement","subkind":"proposition","paper":"2604.07243","version":"3","local":"prop-1","file":"","label":"inlocal","number":"2.1","section":"sec-2","order":2,"title":"Proposition","body_md":"\\label{inlocal}\nEvery commutative ring $R$ with $1$ embeds into the product of its localizations at maximal ideals\n\\[\nS=\\prod_{\\mathfrak m\\in\\mathrm{MaxSpec}(R)} R_{\\mathfrak m}\n\\]\nvia the diagonal map $a\\mapsto \\bigl(\\frac{a}{1}\\bigr)_{\\mathfrak m}$,\nsee, e.g.,~\\cite{AtiyahMacdonald}.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"prop","item":"statement/proposition","head":"environment","counter":"thm","number_from":"counter","labels":["inlocal"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"sha_rigidity_jgcc.tex","from":234,"to":241},"hash":"sha256:fea0486e456538262d73eb8340d8c2f713630ed20da46b7fd038a9690d3d78d6","minhash":"","census":"2604.07243v3#env-2","extractor":"ax/v0.5.19"}
{"tag":"7J6R","kind":"remark","paper":"2604.07243","version":"3","local":"rem-1","file":"","label":"rem:trace","number":"3.1","section":"sec-5","order":3,"title":"Remark","body_md":"\\label{rem:trace}\nSince $\\varphi(g)$ is conjugate to $g$ for every $g\\in E(\\mathbf A_1)$,\nwe will freely use $\\operatorname{tr}(\\varphi(X))=\\operatorname{tr}(X)$ for all $X\\in E(\\mathbf A_1)$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"rem","item":"remark","head":"environment","counter":"thm","number_from":"counter","name":"Trace invariance","labels":["rem:trace"],"scope":"paper","origin":"own","span":{"file":"sha_rigidity_jgcc.tex","from":317,"to":320},"hash":"sha256:e177c96dff5d0542f949671e1d6bc30d2282cf1b23d6510676eb9b6e8e099576","minhash":"","census":"2604.07243v3#env-3","extractor":"ax/v0.5.19"}
{"tag":"CMIO","kind":"statement","subkind":"lemma","paper":"2604.07243","version":"3","local":"lem-1","file":"","label":"lem:cent","number":"3.2","section":"sec-7","order":4,"title":"Lemma","body_md":"\\label{lem:cent}\nThe centralizer of $x_\\alpha(1)$ in $\\mathrm{M}_3(R)$ consists precisely of the matrices\n\\[\nX=\\begin{pmatrix}\na\u0026 b\u0026 2h\\\\\n0\u0026 a\u0026 0\\\\\n0\u0026 h\u0026 a\n\\end{pmatrix}\\qquad (a,b,h\\in R).\n\\]","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"lem","item":"statement/lemma","head":"environment","counter":"thm","number_from":"counter","labels":["lem:cent"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"sha_rigidity_jgcc.tex","from":354,"to":363},"hash":"sha256:e40ed469437e7ddcc0c97c5741ac42f76507c6e71854b3654d9c02a08245bd59","minhash":"","census":"2604.07243v3#env-4","extractor":"ax/v0.5.19"}
{"tag":"FIBL","kind":"statement","subkind":"lemma","paper":"2604.07243","version":"3","local":"lem-2","file":"","label":"lem:impossible","number":"3.3","section":"sec-11","order":5,"title":"Lemma","body_md":"\\label{lem:impossible}\nThe situation\n\\[\nB=\n\\begin{pmatrix}\na(1+hd)\u0026 ah\u0026 0\\\\\nad\u0026 a\u0026 0\\\\\n0\u0026 0\u0026 a\n\\end{pmatrix}\\in G(\\mathbf A_1)\n\\]\nis impossible for $h,d\\neq 0$ and $a\\neq 1$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"lem","item":"statement/lemma","head":"environment","counter":"thm","number_from":"counter","labels":["lem:impossible"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"sha_rigidity_jgcc.tex","from":513,"to":524},"hash":"sha256:02acd6cf20cc7dcb9a230b13af928d2f46d8d5bb2f9bebaa26369701997cac46","minhash":"","census":"2604.07243v3#env-5","extractor":"ax/v0.5.19"}
{"tag":"TVUL","kind":"statement","subkind":"theorem","paper":"2604.07243","version":"3","local":"thm-2","file":"","label":"thm:A1","number":"3.4","section":"sec-13","order":6,"title":"Theorem","body_md":"\\label{thm:A1}\nLet $R$ be a commutative ring with $1/2\\in R$. Then any locally inner endomorphism of\n$E_{\\mathrm{ad}}(\\mathbf A_1,R)$ is inner. Equivalently, $E_{\\mathrm{ad}}(\\mathbf A_1,R)$ has Property~E, hence is $\\operatorname{Sha}$-rigid.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"thm","item":"statement/theorem","head":"environment","counter":"thm","number_from":"counter","labels":["thm:A1"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"sha_rigidity_jgcc.tex","from":599,"to":602},"hash":"sha256:58bb858c7b69ce74525718ac0336495c4cb3150d1c8e756b65b051ebeecc178c","minhash":"","census":"2604.07243v3#env-6","extractor":"ax/v0.5.19"}
{"tag":"K8H1","kind":"remark","paper":"2604.07243","version":"3","local":"rem-2","file":"","number":"3.5","section":"sec-13","order":7,"title":"Remark","body_md":"For the full adjoint Chevalley group $G_{\\mathrm{ad}}(\\mathbf A_1,R)$ the same conclusion follows whenever\n$E_{\\mathrm{ad}}(\\mathbf A_1,R)\\trianglelefteq G_{\\mathrm{ad}}(\\mathbf A_1,R)$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"rem","item":"remark","head":"environment","counter":"thm","number_from":"counter","scope":"paper","origin":"own","span":{"file":"sha_rigidity_jgcc.tex","from":604,"to":607},"hash":"sha256:012cbe5a40368b664d8b7216dad47d9249b5d6382b31462a4960b14c6e969b72","minhash":"","census":"2604.07243v3#env-7","extractor":"ax/v0.5.19"}
{"tag":"FSUG","kind":"statement","subkind":"proposition","paper":"2604.07243","version":"3","local":"prop-2","file":"","label":"prop:CentX0","number":"4.1","section":"sec-16","order":8,"title":"Proposition","body_md":"\\label{prop:CentX0}\n\\[\nC_{G_{\\mathrm{ad}}(\\mathbf A_2,R)}(X_0)\n=\\Bigl\\{\\,x_{\\alpha_1}(a)\\,x_{\\alpha_2}(a)\\,x_{\\alpha_1+\\alpha_2}(b)\\ \\Bigm|\\ a,b\\in R\\,\\Bigr\\}.\n\\]","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"prop","item":"statement/proposition","head":"environment","counter":"thm","number_from":"counter","labels":["prop:CentX0"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"sha_rigidity_jgcc.tex","from":762,"to":767},"hash":"sha256:26a054f3300a2d34a8fd51b5765e82c546d8b54e95e061c9367d0931fa4e85b4","minhash":"","census":"2604.07243v3#env-8","extractor":"ax/v0.5.19"}
{"tag":"FULU","kind":"statement","subkind":"proposition","paper":"2604.07243","version":"3","local":"prop-3","file":"","label":"prop:image-a1+a2","number":"4.2","section":"sec-17","order":9,"title":"Proposition","body_md":"\\label{prop:image-a1+a2}\nLet $X_{12}=\\varphi\\bigl(x_{\\alpha_1+\\alpha_2}(1)\\bigr)$.\nThen\n\\[\nX_{12}=x_{\\alpha_1}(a)\\,x_{\\alpha_2}(a)\\,x_{\\alpha_1+\\alpha_2}(b)\n\\quad\\text{with}\\quad a^2=0\\ \\ \\text{and}\\ \\ b\\in R^\\times.\n\\]","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"prop","item":"statement/proposition","head":"environment","counter":"thm","number_from":"counter","labels":["prop:image-a1+a2"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"sha_rigidity_jgcc.tex","from":844,"to":851},"hash":"sha256:321d8bd92831d849677aa77f48d922ad3691e79e5622055a9ab08612e847e8ef","minhash":"","census":"2604.07243v3#env-9","extractor":"ax/v0.5.19"}
{"tag":"QNN3","kind":"statement","subkind":"proposition","paper":"2604.07243","version":"3","local":"prop-4","file":"","number":"4.3","section":"sec-23","order":10,"title":"Proposition","body_md":"Let $R$ be a commutative ring and let $G_{\\mathrm{ad}}(A_2,R)$ be the adjoint Chevalley group of type~$A_2$ over $R$.\nSet $\\gamma=\\alpha_1+\\alpha_2$ and consider\n\\[\nY \\;=\\; x_{\\alpha_1}(1)\\,w_\\gamma(1)\\,x_{\\alpha_2}(1)\\in G_{\\mathrm{ad}}(A_2,R).\n\\]\nLet $\\varphi$ be the automorphism of $G_{\\mathrm{ad}}(A_2,R)$ such that\n\\[\n\\varphi(x_{\\pm \\alpha_1}(1))=x_{\\pm \\alpha_2}(1),\\qquad\n\\varphi(x_{\\pm \\alpha_2}(1))=x_{\\pm \\alpha_1}(1).\n\\]\nThen, if $R$ has at least one localization by a maximal ideal with residue field of characteristic $\\ne 7$, the elements $Y$ and $\\varphi(Y)$ are not conjugate in $G_{\\mathrm{ad}}(A_2,R)$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"prop","item":"statement/proposition","head":"environment","counter":"thm","number_from":"counter","scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"sha_rigidity_jgcc.tex","from":1382,"to":1394},"hash":"sha256:a6994bf544f2a2ae47e7844dcda9678d20a5c0965ea0076d78e92a0ea24373a7","minhash":"","census":"2604.07243v3#env-10","extractor":"ax/v0.5.19"}
{"tag":"WW0Y","kind":"statement","subkind":"theorem","paper":"2604.07243","version":"3","local":"thm-3","file":"","label":"thm:Sha-elementary-A2","number":"4.4","section":"sec-24","order":11,"title":"Theorem","body_md":"\\label{thm:Sha-elementary-A2}\nLet $R$ be a commutative ring with $1/2\\in R$.\nThen every locally inner endomorphism of the elementary adjoint Chevalley group\n$E_{\\mathrm{ad}}(\\mathbf A_2,R)$ is inner. Equivalently, $E_{\\mathrm{ad}}(\\mathbf A_2,R)$ is $\\operatorname{Sha}$-rigid.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"thm","item":"statement/theorem","head":"environment","counter":"thm","number_from":"counter","labels":["thm:Sha-elementary-A2"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"sha_rigidity_jgcc.tex","from":1522,"to":1526},"hash":"sha256:8559409e605ec26e333895d0b04828305af7765e950bfe2c0f4aabb01a1bf211","minhash":"","census":"2604.07243v3#env-11","extractor":"ax/v0.5.19"}
{"tag":"G0JA","kind":"statement","subkind":"theorem","paper":"2604.07243","version":"3","local":"thm-4","file":"","label":"thm:A2-adjoint","number":"4.5","section":"sec-25","order":12,"title":"Theorem","body_md":"\\label{thm:A2-adjoint}\nLet $R$ be a commutative ring with $1/2\\in R$.\nThen every locally inner endomorphism of the adjoint Chevalley group\n$G_{\\mathrm{ad}}(\\mathbf A_2,R)$ is inner. Equivalently, $G_{\\mathrm{ad}}(\\mathbf A_2,R)$ is $\\operatorname{Sha}$-rigid.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"thm","item":"statement/theorem","head":"environment","counter":"thm","number_from":"counter","labels":["thm:A2-adjoint"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"sha_rigidity_jgcc.tex","from":1535,"to":1539},"hash":"sha256:994bf1751ea5fd486b6efc87ba54814d89c9b9b8ee06f4e1df60a8f0103669a3","minhash":"","census":"2604.07243v3#env-12","extractor":"ax/v0.5.19"}
{"tag":"H826","kind":"statement","subkind":"lemma","paper":"2604.07243","version":"3","local":"lem-3","file":"","label":"lem:B2-cent","number":"5.1","section":"sec-29","order":13,"title":"Lemma","body_md":"\\label{lem:B2-cent}\nThe centralizer of $X_0$ in $U^+$ consists precisely of the elements\n\\[\nx_\\alpha(b)x_\\beta(b)x_{\\alpha+\\beta}\\!\\left(\\frac{b^2-b}{2}\\right)x_{\\alpha+2\\beta}(d),\n\\qquad b,d\\in R.\n\\]","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"lem","item":"statement/lemma","head":"environment","counter":"thm","number_from":"counter","labels":["lem:B2-cent"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"sha_rigidity_jgcc.tex","from":1617,"to":1623},"hash":"sha256:fa1c413d5894703afd7a21bba62d272f7b9e6b0c41b96c01499c52aa9603480b","minhash":"","census":"2604.07243v3#env-13","extractor":"ax/v0.5.19"}
{"tag":"M8RE","kind":"statement","subkind":"lemma","paper":"2604.07243","version":"3","local":"lem-4","file":"","label":"lem:B2-X4","number":"5.2","section":"sec-30","order":14,"title":"Lemma","body_md":"\\label{lem:B2-X4}\nOne has\n\\[\nX_4=\\varphi(x_{\\alpha+2\\beta}(1))=x_{\\alpha+2\\beta}(b)\n\\quad\\text{for some }b\\in R^\\times.\n\\]","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"lem","item":"statement/lemma","head":"environment","counter":"thm","number_from":"counter","labels":["lem:B2-X4"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"sha_rigidity_jgcc.tex","from":1667,"to":1673},"hash":"sha256:6d4ec65612eda065369f99671ceca4133a3733d53d8ca7e8b048be81f9c83308","minhash":"","census":"2604.07243v3#env-14","extractor":"ax/v0.5.19"}
{"tag":"3SMZ","kind":"statement","subkind":"proposition","paper":"2604.07243","version":"3","local":"prop-5","file":"","label":"prop:B2-X3","number":"5.3","section":"sec-31","order":15,"title":"Proposition","body_md":"\\label{prop:B2-X3}\nAfter conjugating $\\varphi$ by an element of the centralizer $C(X_0)$, we may assume\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:B2-X3-form}\nX_3=\nx_\\alpha(s)\\,x_\\beta(s)\\,x_{\\alpha+\\beta}\\!\\left(b+\\frac{s^2-s}{2}\\right),\n\\qquad s\\in\\operatorname{Rad} R_J \\text{ in each localization }R_J.\n\\end{equation}","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"prop","item":"statement/proposition","head":"environment","counter":"thm","number_from":"counter","labels":["prop:B2-X3","eq:B2-X3-form"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"sha_rigidity_jgcc.tex","from":1688,"to":1695},"hash":"sha256:baa9e7e09aab0186c1c2c37e9b0f651d2090640e76ff56d4687ced4dabd0fe19","minhash":"","census":"2604.07243v3#env-15","extractor":"ax/v0.5.19"}
{"tag":"3FVV","kind":"statement","subkind":"theorem","paper":"2604.07243","version":"3","local":"thm-5","file":"","label":"thm:B2-elementary","number":"5.4","section":"sec-35","order":16,"title":"Theorem","body_md":"\\label{thm:B2-elementary}\nLet $R$ be a commutative ring with $1/2\\in R$.\nThen every locally inner endomorphism of $E_{\\mathrm{ad}}(\\mathbf B_2,R)$ is inner.\nEquivalently, $E_{\\mathrm{ad}}(\\mathbf B_2,R)$ is $\\operatorname{Sha}$-rigid.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"thm","item":"statement/theorem","head":"environment","counter":"thm","number_from":"counter","labels":["thm:B2-elementary"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"sha_rigidity_jgcc.tex","from":1839,"to":1843},"hash":"sha256:450ef8c4e5b0b55c09fc4674e569f33d301dc98e494a050e7b0e11e41a3b67ab","minhash":"","census":"2604.07243v3#env-16","extractor":"ax/v0.5.19"}
{"tag":"ED3L","kind":"statement","subkind":"theorem","paper":"2604.07243","version":"3","local":"thm-6","file":"","label":"thm:B2-adjoint","number":"5.5","section":"sec-35","order":17,"title":"Theorem","body_md":"\\label{thm:B2-adjoint}\nLet $R$ be a commutative ring with $1/2\\in R$.\nThen every locally inner endomorphism of $G_{\\mathrm{ad}}(\\mathbf B_2,R)$ is inner.\nEquivalently, $G_{\\mathrm{ad}}(\\mathbf B_2,R)$ is $\\operatorname{Sha}$-rigid.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"thm","item":"statement/theorem","head":"environment","counter":"thm","number_from":"counter","labels":["thm:B2-adjoint"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"elsewhere","origin":"own","span":{"file":"sha_rigidity_jgcc.tex","from":1845,"to":1849},"hash":"sha256:f5b1b6001e34bd128424bd873cb1dc7a5466730a42eb60d0348e6e6854c6e485","minhash":"","census":"2604.07243v3#env-17","extractor":"ax/v0.5.19"}
{"tag":"3QTW","kind":"statement","subkind":"theorem","paper":"2604.07243","version":"3","local":"thm-7","file":"","label":"thm:G2-elementary","number":"6.1","section":"sec-47","order":18,"title":"Theorem","body_md":"\\label{thm:G2-elementary}\nLet $R$ be a commutative ring with $1/2,1/3\\in R$.\nThen every locally inner endomorphism of $E_{\\mathrm{ad}}(\\mathbf G_2,R)$ is inner.\nEquivalently, $E_{\\mathrm{ad}}(\\mathbf G_2,R)$ is $\\operatorname{Sha}$-rigid.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"thm","item":"statement/theorem","head":"environment","counter":"thm","number_from":"counter","labels":["thm:G2-elementary"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"sha_rigidity_jgcc.tex","from":2224,"to":2228},"hash":"sha256:f524110ddb079e98ff51c0e878f59354189486989c7710e850aac8dfc6b8828d","minhash":"","census":"2604.07243v3#env-18","extractor":"ax/v0.5.19"}
{"tag":"QEZF","kind":"statement","subkind":"theorem","paper":"2604.07243","version":"3","local":"thm-8","file":"","label":"thm:G2-adjoint","number":"6.2","section":"sec-47","order":19,"title":"Theorem","body_md":"\\label{thm:G2-adjoint}\nLet $R$ be a commutative ring with $1/2,1/3\\in R$.\nThen every locally inner endomorphism of $G_{\\mathrm{ad}}(\\mathbf G_2,R)$ is inner.\nEquivalently, $G_{\\mathrm{ad}}(\\mathbf G_2,R)$ is $\\operatorname{Sha}$-rigid.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"thm","item":"statement/theorem","head":"environment","counter":"thm","number_from":"counter","labels":["thm:G2-adjoint"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"elsewhere","origin":"own","span":{"file":"sha_rigidity_jgcc.tex","from":2230,"to":2234},"hash":"sha256:aa12475c270fa99cdfec5b3fbc8367d28448f390475374370c99232877fd5f13","minhash":"","census":"2604.07243v3#env-19","extractor":"ax/v0.5.19"}
